:: Pub Gentlemans Club
    <<effects>><<set $xchange.landryGentlemansIntro to 1>>
    "The Gentleman's club?" Landry looks at you, puzzled. <<He>> leans back. "Yes, of course I know about them.
    They are a shadowy organisation dedicated to serving the non-con exhibitionism market."
    <br><br>
    <<He>> takes out a bunch of coins from <<his>> pocket and begins laying them down on the table in a
    grid-like pattern on one side. Then, <<he>> writes "target" on a scrap of paper and places a plain poker chip between them.
    <br><br>
    "Their operation mainly deals with sourcing exploitable individuals and linking them to paying customers
    who'll want to make them do stuff under duress," <<he>> moves the coins to the chip,
    and stacks them neatly, before finally taking a few coins from the top and placing them on the scrap of paper.
    <br><br>
    "They employ the carrot and the stick method, by both blackmailing <i>and rewarding</i> the victims,
    in order to keep them compliant and malleable during the early period in which they are still able to resist,"
    <<he>> explains. "Once the victims are deep enough in trouble, they withhold any and all rewards,
    pocketing them as profit."
    <br><br>
    "It's a cruel business, but an effective one," <<he>> remarks. "People talk too freely after a few drinks.
    I've heard enough to know how it works."
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Ask how <<he>> knows so much|Pub Gentlemans Club 2]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club 2
    <<effects>>
    Landry turns the ordinary poker chip between two fingers as <<he>> studies your expression.
    Then, realisation dawns on <<him>>.
    <br><br>
    "Oh shit. Wait a minute," <<he>> says, lowering <<his>> voice.
    "Those rumours about a popular new target making the rounds among their outer circles.
    That's you, isn't it? No wonder you're asking about them."
    <br><br>
    You tense, but Landry raises both hands. "I don't buy their material, and I'm not one of them.
    Patrons bring rumours through my door, and some of my contacts have crossed paths with their money.
    I hadn't realised the person they were talking about was you."
    <br><br>
    Landry pushes the chip away with a look of distaste. You still have a problem to solve, so you ask what <<he>> can do.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Ask about stopping the blackmail|Pub Gentlemans Club 3]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club 3
    <<effects>>
    Landry scratches <<his>> chin, deep in thought for a few moments.
    "I could lean on the people who move their messages and money. Feed them false leads, bury your name,
    and make it look like watching you is no longer worth the effort."
    <br><br>
    "That's the best I can do," Landry says apologetically. "I can't destroy an organisation that powerful,
    but I can make their information unreliable for a while."
    <br><br>
    You take a breath before inquiring further.
    <br><br>
    "The plan would require <<printprice 1000000>>," <<he>> explains. "Most of it will go to people over whom I hold no sway."
    <br><br>
    You wince involuntarily at the price tag.
    <br><br>
    "Expensive, I know. But you must also understand that this won't be a permanent solution either."
    <<He>> exhales wearily as <<he>> leans forward to whisper. "Look. The club is full of powerful, capricious people,"
    Landry pauses for a moment to think. "This will likely buy you <span class="blue">a month of peace</span>
    at the very least. Perhaps more, but only if you are careful."
    <br><br>
    <<if $money gte (setup.inflation ? setup.inflation.price(1000000) : 1000000)>>
        <<link [[Stop blackmail (<<printprice 1000000>>)|Pub Gentlemans Club Pay]]>>
            <<money -1000000 "blackmailHalt">>
            <<set $xchange.blackmailHalt to 30>>
            <<blackmail-endquest>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
        <</link>>
    <<else>>
        You don't have enough cash.
    <</if>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Later|Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club 4
    <<effects>>
    "Back again about the Gentleman's club?" Landry reclines. "It'll be <<printprice 1000000>>
    to make them take their sights off from you for only a month." <<He>> looks disinterested on the surface.
    But you know this topic makes <<him>> nervous.
    <br><br>
    Pulling the wool over powerful people's eyes is a big risk for anyone to take, so you can understand <<his>>
    legitimate concern.
    <br><br>
    <<if $money gte (setup.inflation ? setup.inflation.price(1000000) : 1000000)>>
        <<link [[Stop blackmail (<<printprice 1000000>>)|Pub Gentlemans Club Pay]]>>
            <<money -1000000 "blackmailHalt">>
            <<set $xchange.blackmailHalt to 30>>
            <<blackmail-endquest>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasMaterial to false>>
            <<set $xchange.blackmail.hasNewMaterial to false>>
        <</link>>
    <<else>>
        You don't have enough cash.
    <</if>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Later|Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club Pay
    <<effects>>
    Landry counts the money and seals it in an envelope. "Every penny goes towards getting their eyes off you.
    If you had any tasks assigned to you, it should now be safe to disregard them. I'll take care of everything."
    <br><br>
    <<He>> looks up for a moment, meeting your eyes. "But you better remember to lay low,
    or you'll sure as debt find yourself back again under their sights."
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Pub Landry]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club Cancel
    <<effects>>
    <<run restoreActiveBlackmailQuest()>>
    <<set _cancelQuest to $xchange.blackmail.activeQuest>>
    <<set _cancelCost to Math.round(blackmailReward(1, false) * 5)>>
    You explain that you've been handed a task you can't see through, and ask whether there's any way out of it.
    <br><br>
    Landry drums <<his>> fingers on the table. "One task? That I can do something about. I know which of their
    runners handles the day's reports. A payment in the right hands, and today's page comes back blank."
    <br><br>
    "It won't please them," <<he>> warns. "They'll keep whatever they're holding over you, and they'll ask again.
    But you won't have anything released over today."
    <br><br>
    <<set _cancelSummary to $xchange.blackmail.hasReadLetter ? getStaticQuestData(_cancelQuest)?.summary : undefined>>
    <<if _cancelSummary>>
        Your task was to <span class="teal"><<print _cancelSummary.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + _cancelSummary.slice(1)>></span>
        <br><br>
    <</if>>
    <<He>> names <<his>> price: <<printmoney _cancelCost>>.
    <br><br>
    <<if $money gte _cancelCost>>
        <<link [[Pay to cancel today's task|Pub Gentlemans Club Cancel Pay]]>>
            <<money `-_cancelCost` "blackmailHalt">>
            <<blackmail-cancelquest>>
        <</link>>
    <<else>>
        You don't have enough cash.
    <</if>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Later|Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse]]>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club Cancel Pay
    <<effects>>
    Landry pockets the money without counting it. "Give me the hour. Whatever they told you to do today,
    forget about it. As far as their records will show, you were never given anything."
    <br><br>
    <span class="green">Today's task has been cancelled.</span> <<He>> holds up a finger before you can thank <<him>>.
    "Once. Don't make a habit of it. They notice patterns, and I'd rather they didn't start looking at me."
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Pub Landry]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
    <br>

:: Pub Gentlemans Club Refuse
    <<effects>>
    "Very well, then." Landry leans back into <<his>> chair. "As you prefer. Let me know if you change your mind."
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Pub Landry]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
    <br>
